# Test: under system dns-source mode merge, Ze lists the IPCP lease's DNS
#       server and then system name-server, and its own lookups reach the
#       configured server when the lease's server does not answer.
# Spec: spec-home-cpe-23-dns-source-fall-through -- AC-17
# VALIDATES: the merge mode of the shared rule (dnssource.Select,
#            internal/core/dnssource/select.go) through the daemon: the
#            registry (Resolvers.refresh, internal/component/config/system/resolv.go)
#            writes resolv.conf and hands the same selection to the internal
#            resolver (newResolvers, cmd/ze/hub/main_system.go), which asks each
#            server in order. The compiled fixture first waits until the file
#            lists the host's own /etc/resolv.conf servers then 198.51.100.53
#            (no lease yet: the host record is the received fallback, D-13,
#            and a QEMU guest names its slirp resolver there), then plays the access
#            concentrator on zeac0 (internal/test/pppoeac) and Naks the client's
#            Primary-DNS request with 192.0.2.53 (IPCPWithDNS, RFC 1877 Section
#            1.1). The file must then list 192.0.2.53 then 198.51.100.53 (the
#            lease's record replaces the host fallback), and
#            only after that does the fixture ask `show dns lookup
#            web.example.test type A`, which must answer 203.0.113.10.
#            Nothing listens on 192.0.2.53, so that answer comes from the
#            configured server after the first one refused.
# PREVENTS: a merge list that stops at the first source holding a server, as
#           first-usable does, and a resolver that asks only its first server.
#
# 192.0.2.53 and 198.51.100.53 sit on dummy links of the per-test namespace;
# only 198.51.100.53 runs the stub. The lease's server is not a loopback
# address because the PPPoE client adopts only a global unicast DNS server
# (adoptNakDNS, internal/component/l2tp/pppoeclient/session.go). The stub
# binds port 53 because system name-server carries no port. The daemon
# refuses a relative resolv-conf-path at config validation (ze:validate
# "resolv-conf-path", internal/component/config/validators_resolvconf.go), so the path
# is /proc/self/cwd/<name>: absolute, yet inside the daemon's working
# directory, the runner's fresh per-test directory. The fixture is the
# daemon's plugin and runs in that directory too (ConfigDir of a stdin
# config is the daemon's cwd), so it reads the bare name. The suite is pppoe,
# not plugin, because only a per-test-namespace suite honours
# option=netns-link.
#
# Requires Linux, CAP_NET_ADMIN for the PPP device, CAP_NET_RAW for both
# AF_PACKET sockets and CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for the stub. keepalive interval
# 3600 keeps Echo-Requests off the wire while the fixture negotiates.
option=needs-linux:caps=net-admin,net-raw,net-bind
option=netns-link:name=zecpe0:peer=zeac0
option=netns-link:name=zedns0:address=192.0.2.53/32
option=netns-link:name=zedns2:address=198.51.100.53/32
option=timeout:value=90s

stdin=ze-conf:terminator=EOF_CONF
system {
	name-server [ 198.51.100.53 ]
	dns-source {
		source [ received configured ]
		mode merge
	}
	dns {
		resolv-conf-path "/proc/self/cwd/dns-source-router-merge.resolv.conf";
	}
}

plugin {
	external dns-source-router-merge-test {
		run "le test fixture pppoe/dns-source-router-merge"
		encoder json
	}
}

interface {
	backend netlink
	pppoe-client zedns1 {
		source-interface zecpe0
		authentication {
			username subscriber
			password secret
		}
		mtu 1450
		keepalive {
			interval 3600
			failures 255
		}
		reconnect {
			delay-min 1
			delay-max 1
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=background:seq=1:exec=le mock dns --port 53 --address 198.51.100.53
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-conf:timeout=90s
expect=exit:code=0

# NO NEEDLE MAY HOLD A COLON: the runner splits a directive on ':'.
expect=stderr:contains=web.example.test type A -> records 203.0.113.10 status NOERROR through the configured server after the lease's server refused
reject=stderr:pattern=panic
reject=stderr:pattern=fatal error
